---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import StandardCard from "../../components/StandardCard.astro";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code="IAS 16"
  title="Property, Plant and Equipment"
  category="Assets"
  objective="Prescribe the accounting treatment for property, plant and equipment so that users of financial statements can understand an entity's investment in PPE and changes in that investment."
  principle="Recognise PPE when it is probable that future economic benefits will flow to the entity and the cost of the asset can be measured reliably."
  scope={[
    "Tangible non-current assets",
    "Used in production, supply of goods or services, rental to others, or administrative purposes",
    "Expected to be used for more than one accounting period"
  ]}
>

  <div class="standard-cards-grid">

<StandardCard
  number="01"
  title="Initial Measurement"
  color="blue"
>

  PPE is initially measured at cost.

  Cost includes:

  <ul>
    <li>Purchase price (net of discounts)</li>
    <li>Directly attributable costs</li>
    <li>Initial estimate of dismantling and restoration costs</li>
  </ul>

</StandardCard>

<StandardCard
  number="02"
  title="Depreciation"
  color="green"
>

  Depreciation is the systematic allocation of depreciable amount over useful life.

  <ul>
    <li>Starts when available for use</li>
    <li>Continues even if asset is idle</li>
    <li>Stops on derecognition</li>
  </ul>

  Common methods:

  <ul>
    <li>Straight-line</li>
    <li>Reducing balance</li>
    <li>Units of production</li>
  </ul>

</StandardCard>

<StandardCard
  number="03"
  title="Revaluation"
  color="orange"
>

  Optional accounting policy.

  <ul>
    <li>Entire class of assets must be revalued</li>
    <li>Carrying amount adjusted to fair value</li>
    <li>Revalue regularly</li>
  </ul>

  Increase:
  OCI → Revaluation Surplus

  <br /><br />

  Decrease:
  SOPL unless previous surplus exists

</StandardCard>

<StandardCard
  number="04"
  title="Derecognition"
  color="red"
>

  Remove asset on disposal or when no future economic benefits are expected.

  <br /><br />

  Gain / Loss on disposal:

  <ul>
    <li>Proceeds</li>
    <li>Less: Carrying Amount</li>
  </ul>

  Recognised in SOPL.

</StandardCard>
```

  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
